-- `l4 verify` reads each call through, and joins the atoms of what it reads into
-- the caller's by atomId. `f a` and `f b` each unfold into `loop 3`, where `loop`
-- is a recursive WHERE local that cannot be inlined, so both copies keep the
-- local's one name though one reads a and the other b. Keyed by that name, they
-- were one atom, and `top`, which is TRUE for a = TRUE, b = FALSE, was reported
-- unsatisfiable (found by adversarial review of smucclaw/l4-ide#1013).
-- `same` is the control: there the two copies ARE one proposition.

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE f x IF loop 3
  WHERE
    GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
    GIVETH A BOOLEAN
    loop n MEANS IF n EQUALS 0 THEN x ELSE loop (n - 1)

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE top IF f a AND NOT f b

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE same IF f a AND NOT f a

#EVAL top TRUE FALSE
